From: Anton Argirov <anton.argirov@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:45:25 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(audio): initialize DAC to its neutral level

Unsigned 8-bit DAC silence is 128. Initialize that level both at startup
and on CPU reset to avoid a false full-scale output before the first write.

---
 src/audio/audio.c | 2 +-
 src/cpu.c         | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/audio.c b/src/audio/audio.c
index fa84b8a..a15eb18 100644
--- a/src/audio/audio.c
+++ b/src/audio/audio.c
@@ -711,7 +711,7 @@ char audio_valor_enviar_sonido_izquierdo;
 char audio_valor_enviar_sonido_derecho;
 
 
-z80_byte audiodac_last_value_data;
+z80_byte audiodac_last_value_data=128;
 
 z80_bit audiodac_enabled={0};
 
diff --git a/src/cpu.c b/src/cpu.c
index b0c7b60..5c80e81 100644
--- a/src/cpu.c
+++ b/src/cpu.c
@@ -1014,6 +1014,7 @@ void reset_cpu(void)
 
 
     debug_printf (VERBOSE_INFO,"Reset cpu");
+    audiodac_last_value_data=128;
 
     if (esxdos_umount_on_reset.v) {
         if (esxdos_handler_enabled.v) {
-- 
2.56.0

